unt and  that's not how ours works so how much so  four predefined machine types you'll get  37 percent off for one-year discount for  one-year commitment and for three years  you'll get 55 percent these numbers are  actually a little bit higher for a  custom machine type they're 40 and 57  respectively so the way that we make  that flexible is that the whole thing is  designed based on the underlying  resources so if you think back a minute  ago when I was talking about sustained  use discounts and how s UD 2.0 looks at  the number of cores and RAM that you've  used committed use discounts are the  same way so rather than trying to  predict how many machines you need of a  certain size in what zone just tell us  how much CPU and how much RAM and then  you can use those in any combination so  it sounds like we're asking you to tell  us more but it's actually simpler  because most customers already know that  math  additionally then like I said they're  not tied to any particular VM shape but  they're also not tied to any particular  VM instance itself so what we do is we  simply look at how much was running at  every moment in time every minute and we  take the first chunk of that and we give  you committed use discount on it but the  thing then is whatever's above that we  still give you permanent billing and  sustained use discount on all the rest  so there's no penalty to having a  committed use discount as long as that  is the minimum that you're going to be  using because you're still going to get  the full discounts on all the rest so if  you're not sure how much to buy start  small  see how your workload is running and  then you can increase over time if you  need to and you can know that you're  still getting a really competitive  discount on the rest of it so I built a  little example just to show you what  that looks like very simply in this  picture if you imagine that there's a  threshold where you have a certain  amount of committed use and then above  